# Julia: Manifest.toml records a resolved env. For a package (not an
# application) it must NOT be committed — a committed Manifest resolved on
# newest Julia fails the lts CI job, and its git-tree-sha1 hashes trip the
# detect-secrets pre-commit hook. Ignore it across every environment.
Manifest.toml
**/Manifest.toml
**/Manifest-*.toml

# Generated documentation output and dependencies.
docs/build/
docs/node_modules/
docs/package-lock.json
# README-derived, benchmark, and API-reference pages are generated by
# docs/make.jl.
docs/src/index.md
docs/src/benchmarks.md
docs/src/overall_trend.png
docs/src/lib/public.md
docs/src/lib/internals.md
# The release-notes page (from the repo's GitHub releases) and the
# Literate-rendered tutorial markdown are also generated by docs/make.jl.
docs/src/release-notes.md
docs/src/{{TUTORIALS_SUBDIR}}/*.md

# Coverage artefacts.
*.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.cov
*.jl.mem
coverage/
lcov.info
lcov-*.info

# Benchmark artefacts.
/.benchmarkci
/benchmark/*.json
results_*.json*
tune.json

# Editor / OS clutter.
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# Development worktrees. `worktree-*` covers a sibling-style checkout; the
# convention here is a nested `worktrees/<name>/` under the repo root, which
# the glob doesn't match — a live worktree sat untracked, one `git add -A`
# away from being committed (#247).
worktree-*
worktrees/
